Kotlin Tutorial

  This tutorial demonstrates writing OfficeFloor REST endpoint logic in Kotlin within a Spring
  Boot application.  Because Kotlin compiles to JVM bytecode, Kotlin top-level functions work
  directly as OfficeFloor service procedures alongside Java code.

  {{{https://github.com/officefloor/OfficeFloor/tree/master/tutorials/springboot/KotlinHttpServer}Tutorial Source}}



*Maven dependency

  Add the OfficeFloor Kotlin support alongside the Spring Boot starter:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/pom.xml|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Application class

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/kotlin/net/officefloor/tutorial/kotlinhttpserver/Application.kt|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Kotlin service function

  The Kotlin top-level function that handles the request uses <<<@RequestBody>>> for the request
  body and <<<ObjectResponse>>> to send the response:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/kotlin/net/officefloor/tutorial/kotlinhttpserver/KotlinLogic.kt|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*REST endpoint

  The YAML file routes <<<POST '/'>>> to the Kotlin function via the <<<Kotlin>>> procedure
  source.  The compiled class name for a Kotlin file of top-level functions is <<<\<filename\>Kt>>>:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/index.POST.yml|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Kotlin data classes

  Kotlin data classes work directly as JSON request and response objects.  Jackson's Kotlin module
  (included via <<<officekotlin>>>) handles serialisation automatically:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/kotlin/net/officefloor/tutorial/kotlinhttpserver/KotlinRequest.kt|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/kotlin/net/officefloor/tutorial/kotlinhttpserver/KotlinResponse.kt|ignoreDownloadError=false}



